issue.body:
On Windows, 32bit binaries with VC10,
when trying to create a window with a size bigger than the resolution of one screen, the creation fails with the following message:

```
Failed to share the OpenGL context
```

I only have one graphics card, 3 screens all plugged in, and I'm trying to create a window with no border that would cover the entire three screens.

Here is a code snippet that reproduces the bug on my setup:

``` c++
#include <SFML/Graphics.hpp>

int main(){
  sf::Window lWindow(sf::VideoMode(5760, 1080, 16), "Test", sf::Style::None);

  lWindow.setFramerateLimit(30);

  while(lWindow.isOpen()){

    lWindow.display();
  }

}
```

edit : it actually seems quite linked to Issue #215,
Except the window is not just limited to desktop size but to a one-screen size (which, after testing, seems to be the smallest size among all screens).
I also would like to add that I managed to get an opengl context covering the entire three screens with my own windowing system, so this issue should not be an OS limitation.
